      "evidence": "[L1] states: \"With the identity chart, $\\ell^\\infty$ is a Banach manifold modelled on itself\", citing def-countable-base-banach-manifold-and-smooth-map. That item defines a Banach manifold only \"when additionally $M$ is Hausdorff ... and second countable\", and its Remark insists \"The pair (Hausdorff, second countable) is part of the definition and is never dropped below\"; the published rem-manifold-conventions-and-the-role-of-second-countability records the same convention (\"Some authors ... add countability only when they need it; this library does not\"). But $\\ell^\\infty$ is not second countable: the uncountably many 0-1 sequences are pairwise at sup-distance 1, so any dense set is uncountable ($f \\mapsto d_f$ with $\\|d_f-f\\|<1/3$ is injective on them), hence $\\ell^\\infty$ is not separable and, under the AC_omega the item assumes (thm-metric-countability-equivalences), not second countable. So [L1] is false, and since def-split-banach-submanifold defines \"split $C^k$ submanifold of $M$\" only for a $C^k$ Banach manifold $M$ (\"let $M$ be a $C^k$ Banach manifold modelled on the real Banach space $E$\"), the Statement \"$c_0$ ... is not a split Banach submanifold of $\\ell^\\infty$\" is not covered by the cited definition. The same claim recurs in the Remark of def-split-banach-submanifold (\"the companion page exhibits a closed subspace of $\\ell^\\infty$ that is not a split submanifold of it\"); the local splitting argument of steps 2.1-5.1 stays valid as a statement about charts of $\\ell^\\infty$, but the ambient is not a Banach manifold in the library's sense.",
